  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase 1 of the Middle East Humanitarian Appeal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IRPAL plan came in response to actual needs and is driven by the people in-crisis as direct needs, priorities and preferences, and, by the local context and humanitarian system current gaps as indirect drivers of marginalization, vulnerability and suffering. Accordingly, Gaza response aims to contribute at two levels:A) at the response level, in which it contributes to lifesaving, inclusive, safe and dignified protection, andB) long-term access to daily multisectoral needs of people in crisis in the Gaza Strip. And at the humanitarian system level, by boosting and fostering coordination between IRPAL and DEC&apos;s partners as well as respective local partners based on learning, sharing and disseminating learnings on people-driven actual data on their needs, priorities and preferences towards more inclusive, protective and actual-needs based humanitarian action.IRPAL response aims to complement DEC partners efforts in reducing immediate suffering by providing urgent assistance (outcome 2.0) and providing protection support (outcome 1.0) to crisis-affected people in the Gaza Strip. The overarching objective is to contribute to resilience and improved humanitarian conditions, safety and dignity of conflict-affected people in the Gaza Strip).This approach will ultimately contribute to the safety, dignity, and resilience of crisis-affected people by enhancing protection (outcome 1.0) and access to lifesaving provisions. By transforming negative coping mechanisms  into positive adaptive capacities (outcome 2.0), we strive to foster improved humanitarian conditions and overall wellbeing.The proposed intervention aims to provide life-saving support to conflict affected displaced communities by addressing their immediate food and non-food needs, including ready-to-eat food parcels and essential NFIs including but not limited to (blankets, mattresses, pillows, hygiene kits, baby kits, adult diapers and kitchen sets, etc.)This intervention will prioritize the most vulnerable populations, such as children, pregnant and lactating women, older people and people with disabilities, who are often disproportionately affected by conflict and displacement. By addressing immediate needs for food and essential items, IR Lebanon (IRL) aims to alleviate suffering and promote dignity among those impacted by crisis. This immediate and life-saving support will assist communities particularly vulnerable groups to maintain their lives with dignity and respect. Overall objective of the assistance is to provide relief to those who have been forced to flee their homes due to the current conflict. Through this intervention, IRL aim to ensure that the basic needs are met and that individuals can begin to rebuild their lives in a safe and secure environment. This support will help alleviate the burden on already strained resources and enable vulnerable populations to access the assistance they require.</narrative>
  </description>
